# Update docs on relevant changes

When shipping a feature, fix, or refactor that changes **observable behavior**, include doc updates in the same commit:

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Bot commands, capture flow, inbox | `CLAUDE.md` § Bot Telegram |
| New/removed env vars | `.env.example` + `CLAUDE.md` if non-obvious |
| API endpoints, module behavior | `CLAUDE.md` module section |
| Architecture decisions | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Infra/deploy | `CLAUDE.md` § Infraestructura (+ homelab repo if server-side) |

`CLAUDE.md` is the living source of truth for current state. `docs/architecture.md` is reference for decisions and conventions.

Skip doc updates only for pure internals with no user-facing or operator-facing impact.
